<https://spdx.org/rdf/3/terms/Core/ExternalIdentifierType/ibrn> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "International Business Registration Number (IBRN) <https://ekys.org/business_identifiers/> is a unique identifier for legal entities standardized by ISO 8000-116 <https://www.iso.org/standard/75117.html>. It is composed of two parts: a jurisdiction prefix and a local authoritative legal entity identifier (ALEI), separated by a colon. The prefix contains an ISO 3166 country code, an optional subdivision code, and a register code (e.g., US-DE.BER:3031657)."@en .
<https://spdx.org/rdf/3/terms/Core/ExternalIdentifierType/iswc> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "International Standard Musical Work Code (ISWC) <https://www.iswc.org/iswc> is an 11-character unique identifier standardized by ISO 15707 <https://www.iso.org/standard/83125.html> for musical works (compositions) as distinct from specific recordings. While the \"ISWC\" label and grouping separators (dots and hyphens) are used for human readability, they shall be omitted when the identifier is stored electronically (e.g., T0017812031)."@en .
